      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "16 Cabinteely Way is a fantastic extended 4 bedroom semi-detached family home located in this ever-popular location in Cabinteely. The property measures approx. 141m2 and is presented in excellent condition throughout, this home is ideally situated close to a host of local amenities and schools, making it the ideal family home.\n\nOn entering this bright property there is an immediate sense of light and space. At ground floor level the accommodation comprises; entrance hall, living room, open plan kitchen/breakfast room, study/office and guest wc. On the first floor there are four generously proportioned double bedrooms and a family bathroom. \n\nConveniently located close to Cabinteely Village, Deansgrange, Dun Laoghaire, Stillorgan and Blackrock. The property enjoys easy access to a wide range of local amenities including shops, cafés, restaurants, schools, parks, and excellent transport links. Cabinteely Park is located nearby and is an attractive public facility for walks and outdoor sports. Dunnes Stores in the Cornelscourt Shopping Centre is also within walking distance. The surrounding area is particularly popular with families thanks to recreational facilities and proximity to some of South Dublin's most respected schools including; Loreto Foxrock, Blackrock College, Clonkeen College, Cabinteely Community School, St. Brigid's and Johnstown National School. UCD and Trinity College are also a short distance away via public transport and the N11.\n\nFeatures:\n\n• Extended four-bedroom family home \n• Excellent condition throughout. \n• Gas fire central heating. \n• Off street car parking to the front \n• Close to a selection of shops, restaurants, and schools. \n• Close to N11 and M50. \n• Approx. 141m2 (1517sqft).\n\nAccommodation Details:\n\nGround Floor: \n\nEntrance Hall: 5.78m x 2.30m \nA large entrance hall with wooden floor. Understairs storage. Coving. Recess lighting.\n\nLiving Room: 5.8m9 x 3.35m \nSolid fuel burner (back boiler). Wooden floor. Coving. \n\nKitchen/Dining Area: 7.30m x 3.30m \nLarge bright room. A large range of presses and storage. Oven and hob. Fridge freezer. Dishwasher. Wooden floor. Recess lighting. Sliding patio door to rear garden. \n\nFamily Room/Office: 5.93m x 2.34m \nRecess lighting. Tv point.\nGuest w.c: \nWc, whb. Wooden floor.\n\nFirst Floor: \n\nLanding: 3.51m x 2.29m\nVelux window. Access to attic. Hotpress and storage.\n\nBedroom 1: 3.78 x 2.76m \nDouble bedroom overlooking the rear garden. Fitted double wardrobes. \n\nEnsuite: 1.83m x 1.70m\nWc. Whb. Corner shower. Tiled floors and walls. Recess lighting.\n\nBedroom 2: 4.05m x 3.34m \nDouble bedroom. Fitted wardrobes. \n\nBedroom 3: 3.82m x 2.34m \nDouble bedroom. Fitted wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 4: 4.05m x 3.34m \nDouble bedroom. Fitted wardrobe.\n\nBathroom: 3.40m x 2.34m \nWc, whb. Bath. Corner shower with electric shower. Heated towel rail. Tiled floor.\n\nOutside: \n\nOff street parking. Large lawn rear garden, approx. 16m in depth. Covered patio/BBQ area. Concrete shed. Large decked area."
      },
